[[31,63,0,"<aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/768.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000166.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>FOLLOW ALL THE RECOMMENDED SAFETY\nFULES (<a href=\"#/3025608\">5580C</a> ).</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside>"],[31,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>Lift the seat to the end of\nits travel.</p><p>1. Move the seat fully forward and undo the rear bolts.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2005352.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[31,63,0,"<p>1. Move the seat fully back and undo the front bolts.</p><p>2. Raise the seat slightly, undo retainer (2a) and turn connector\ncarrier bracket (2b) until it is accessible.</p><p>3. Disconnect the electrical connections (3a, 3b, 3c).</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>3a</p></td><td><p>Driver&#x27;s Side Bag</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3024689\">Q30</a></p></td></tr></table></div><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>3a</p></td><td><p>Passenger Side Bag</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3024692\">Q31</a></p></td></tr></table></div><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>3b</p></td><td><p>Driver&#x27;s seat coupling</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3024016\">D70</a></p></td></tr></table></div><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>3b</p></td><td><p>Passenger seat coupling</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3024018\">D71</a></p></td></tr></table></div><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>3c</p></td><td><p>Seat belts warning light switch</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3024174\">I45</a></p></td></tr></table></div><p>4. Remove the seat.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2005353.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[31,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the seat is not\ndamaged.</p><p>1. Connect the electrical connection.</p><p>2. Turn connector carrier bracket (2a) in its seat and do up retainer\n(2b).</p><p>3. Place the seat (3a) in its housing on the floor of the vehicle.\nEnsure it is fully back on the guides and  engage locating  pin\n(2b).</p><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Check that the carpet is not fouling\nagainst the guide support areas. Work with due caution so as not\nto damage the plastic parts.</p></aside><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/768.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000166.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>During this stage do not slide\nthe seat with the backrest folded over.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2005354.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[31,63,0,"<p>1. Screw on and tighten the inner front bolt.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>FRONT SEAT ASSEMBLY.</p></td><td><p>M8</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>2.4</p></td></tr></table></div><p>2. Screw on and tighten the outer front bolt.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>2</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>FRONT SEAT ASSEMBLY.</p></td><td><p>M8</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>2.4</p></td></tr></table></div><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/768.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000166.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>The seat must be fixed to the\nfloor without suffering distortion on the guides. If necessary, adjust\nthe floating nuts making sure that they are free.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2005355.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[31,63,0,"<p>Slide the seat fully forward.\nMake sure that the elements for both guides engage simultaneously.</p><p>1. Screw on and tighten the outer rear bolt.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>FRONT SEAT ASSEMBLY.</p></td><td><p>M8</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>2.4</p></td></tr></table></div><p>2. Screw on and tighten the inner rear bolt.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>2</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>FRONT SEAT ASSEMBLY.</p></td><td><p>M8</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>2.4</p></td></tr></table></div><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/768.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2000166.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th colspan=\"1\"><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>At this stage, do not raise the\nseat to gain access to the bolt; the bracket is slotted.</p></aside></th></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan=\"1\"></td></tr></table></div></aside><p>3. Check that the seat slides correctly. If there is longitudinal\nclearance for the guide attachment, loosen the door side bolts,\nslide and attach the seat several times, then tighten the bolts\nto the recommended torque.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2005356.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[31,63,0,"<p>Check that the seat slides\ncorrectly and that the seat belt unfastened warning light comes\non properly.</p>"]]